{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Hear now, you</b> — I have seen an interpreter [who says] that the high priest returns to Yehotzadak, not to Yehoshua, for he said that he served in filthiness [referring to the dirty garments of v. 3], and he did not explain correctly, for then I showed him the words of the angel to Yehoshua — this verse, which calls him the high priest himself." "<b>and your fellows</b> — they are the rest of the priests, who are worthy to sit before Him, for he is the high priest." "<b>for men of sign</b> — they are worthy that a sign be done for them." "<b>Branch</b> — he is Zerubbabel, as it says [in 6:12], 'Branch is his name,' and the end of the section proves it: 'before Zerubbabel.' And many interpreters said: this Branch is the Messiah, and he is called Zerubbabel because he is of his seed, like [Ezekiel 34:24], 'and David My servant, prince to them forever.' I too have made a way of derash: for Tzemach in gematria is Menachem, and he is the son of Amiel."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The referent of the unspecified interpreter (המפרש) is unknown; the phrase 'I have seen an interpreter' is rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:57.251367494Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}